<h1>sparrow_auth</h1>

<p>A bare Rails application with the engine mounted at <code>/auth</code>. Nothing
here is the engine's own; it is the host side, which is why the mailbox lives
here and not in the gem.</p>

<% if @offer_passkey %>
  <div class="offer">
    <strong>Add a passkey?</strong>
    <p>You are signed in as <%= @current_account.email %> and have no passkey yet.
    A passkey signs you in with this device — Touch ID, Windows Hello, your phone —
    and there is nothing to type and nothing to intercept.</p>
    <p>
      <a href="/auth/webauthn-setup">Add a passkey</a> ·
      <%= button_to "Not now", decline_passkey_path %>
    </p>
  </div>
<% elsif @current_account&.passkey? %>
  <p class="offer-done">Signed in as <%= @current_account.email %>, with
  <%= pluralize(@current_account.webauthn_credentials.count, "passkey") %>.
  <a href="/auth/passkeys">Manage them</a>.</p>
<% end %>

<h2>Try it</h2>
<ol>
  <li><a href="/auth/create-account">Create an account</a>, then open the
      <%= link_to "mailbox", mailbox_path %> and follow the confirmation link.
      It will not confirm until you press the button on the page it opens.</li>
  <li><a href="/auth/otp">Sign in with a code</a>. The code arrives in the
      <%= link_to "mailbox", mailbox_path %>. Note that the same screen appears
      whether or not the address has an account.</li>
  <li>Try an address that does not exist, and one that never confirmed. The page
      says the same thing every time; the mailbox says what actually happened.</li>
  <li><a href="/auth/logout">Sign out</a> and check the session row disappears.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Accounts</h2>
<% if @accounts.any? %>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Address</th><th>Status</th><th>Sessions</th><th>Passkeys</th></tr>
    <% @accounts.each do |account| %>
      <tr>
        <td><%= account.email %></td>
        <td><%= account.verified? ? "confirmed" : "not confirmed" %></td>
        <td><%= ActiveRecord::Base.connection.select_value(
                  ActiveRecord::Base.sanitize_sql_array([
                    "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sparrow_auth_account_active_session_keys WHERE account_id = ?",
                    account.id])) %></td>
        <td><%= account.webauthn_credentials.count %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </table>
<% else %>
  <p>No accounts yet.</p>
<% end %>

<h2>Getting in your way</h2>
<p>One send per address per minute is correct in production and tedious by hand.</p>
<%= button_to "Clear rate limit counters", clear_rate_limits_path %>
